# FEx Framework

## Project Context

FEx (FlakEssentials) is a shared .NET library framework used as a git submodule across projects (DotNetMate, miGit, etc.).

## Architecture

```
FEx.Agnostics.Abstractions     - Framework-independent interfaces
FEx.Agnostics                  - Framework-independent implementations
FEx.DependencyInjection.Abstractions
FEx.DependencyInjection        - Multi-DI (StrongInject + MS DI)
FEx.Core.Abstractions
FEx.Core
FEx.Logging.Abstractions
FEx.Logging                    - IFExLogger (Serilog backend)
FEx.Common.Abstractions
FEx.Common                     - Top layer
```

### File Placement Guidelines
- **FEx.Something.Abstractions** - Extension methods, interfaces, abstract classes, simple records/DTOs
- **FEx.Something** - Complex logic, services, implementations
- **Collection types** - `FEx.Agnostics.Collections`
- **Exception types** - `FEx.Agnostics.Exceptions`
- **Core framework concepts** - `FEx.Core.Abstractions`

## Technical Guidelines

- **Multi-target**: net10.0, netstandard2.0, netstandard2.1, net481 (via MSBuild properties in DevConfigs/Directory.Build.props)
- **Naming**: Projects = `FEx.<Feature>`, new folders without `FEx.` prefix (e.g., `src/Sqlx/FEx.Sqlx.csproj`)
- **Abstractions**: Always in separate projects - interfaces in Abstractions, implementations in main project
- **DI**: StrongInject + Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection, `IInitializeModule<>` / `InitializeModule<,>`
- **MVVM**: CommunityToolkit.Mvvm (`FEx.MVVM`) and ReactiveUI (`FEx.MVVM.Rx`)
- **Logging**: `IFExLogger` / Serilog
- **Build**: NUKE 10.1.0 (`FEx.Building`)
- **API Surface**: Generate with `.\Generate-ApiSurface.ps1 -RepoPath .` (per-project TOML files in `.api-surface/`)

## Build & Test

```powershell
dotnet build FEx.slnx -c Release    # 0 errors expected
dotnet test FEx.slnx                # 38 tests (14 DI + 6 Logging + 18 Flurlx)
```

## Work Tracking

- `work/STATUS.md` - Build/test status snapshot
- `work/OPEN-ISSUES.md` - Active issues
- `work/BACKLOG.md` - Pending specs
- `work/SESSION-LOG.md` - AI session history

## AI Guidelines

- Preserve ALL original comments and XML docs
- Never add explanatory comments to existing code
- Ask when unsure about architecture or business logic
- Build test after each significant change
- Check `work/OPEN-ISSUES.md` for known issues before investigating
